meta {
  name: subscription-revamp
}

docs {
  # Subscription revamp: cancel and refund (ENG-355), external payments and partial billing (ENG-1134),
  # plan selection and change (ENG-690)

  A staging journey over one throw-away test torg. It checks the contract (statuses, role rules, flag
  gating) and that **the money reconciles**: previews match what is actually charged or refunded, wallet and
  advance move by exactly the expected amounts, and a billing's total is always the sum of its line items.

  Errors come back as HTTP 200 with the real code in the body `statusCode`, so every request asserts on the body.

  ## The flags (read this first)

  Everything new sits behind DynamicConfig flags in namespace `subscription-billing`, which are **global to the
  environment**. `PUT /api/v1/config/{namespace}` REPLACES the whole namespace config.

  - Steps 10-26 run with the flags OFF (every flagged route must refuse with 403; legacy routes keep working).
  - Step 30 turns them on (dueSweep stays off: it auto-debits wallets every hour). Steps 31-281 run in the window.
  - Step 300 turns them off again. **Always run 300**, even if something failed. 301-304 prove it.
  - 305-308 end the test torg's subscription and check the flag-off refusal of a CANCELLED subscription.
  - 310-318 read the admin audit log (`GET /api/admin-audit-logs`): the writes above produced rows, GETs did not, refusals
    are DENIED, a non-VAHN_ADMIN gets 403, and no request body or sensitive value is stored.

  ## Status (staging re-run 2026-11-05 on build #1111 / 30d04c6d9, which contains the d7a31e277 billing-insert fix)

  Every group has run on staging against real billings on test torg 685, except the daily `unbilledTruckCheck` pass (no
  request exists: it only runs from a once-a-day timer, about 7 hours after each restart). Steps 140-145 (TRIAL selection)
  ran on 2026-11-04, the rest on 2026-11-05. Two expectations (172, 181) were wrong on first run (a stale advance reading,
  and a refund that is pro-rata after day 1) and were corrected afterwards from the rules; their numbers matched the rules by
  hand but those two requests were not re-run. The journey is single-use per torg.

  Findings from that run:
  - Wallet text for an add-on that is paid in full reads "Subscription payment for billing period X to Y" instead of
    "Subscription add-on: n truck(s), d days, X to Y" (step 205). The part-payment variant works (step 211). The text
    is built after the payment row is recorded COMPLETED, so the ledger already counts it as paid.
  - Step 06: with the flags off, mark-as-verified already reconciles and charges the new truck, so a second reconcile is 400.
  - The scheduler tick that bills a torg whose trial ends decides how the billing is made: with the flags off it is a
    legacy-maths billing charged from the wallet only (advance untouched). Turn the flags on before the tick (steps 150-156).

  ## Status (staging re-run 2026-11-05 evening, build #1117 / af301e40c, torg 712)

  Steps 1-154 passed (122 requests, 69 tests, 125 assertions). 155-281 ran with the scheduler's flags-off second billing: 91 of 101 requests
  passed. Known open items:
  - 193 (static-token cycle change) got 400 "reason is required": an admin-made plan change needs a reason. The request now sends one; it was
    not re-run, and 194-196, 204, 221, 260 and 275-277 failed as a chain from it (the plan stayed monthly).
  - 252: with the static token the billing's cancelled_by is null but the REFUND line items get created_by 1
    (SubscriptionRefundService uses actor.getId() instead of JwtAuthenticator.actorId). Plutus bug, not fixed.
  - 310-318 (admin audit log) passed 11 of 11 requests.

  ## Zeus-screen and wallet checks (steps 320-368, staging 2026-11-06, build #1121 / 228b0b12d)

  Steps 320-333 call the routes the new zeus screens use, with the static VAHN_ADMIN token and `?src=zeus`; 350-368 are the billing-dependent ones.
  They need a torg with a live billing (the scheduler's tick), run inside the step-30 flag window, and are single-use per billing.
  - 320-333 passed (16 of 16 requests, 17 of 17 tests). The storage upload (333) is accepted for the static token.
  - 340-342 (wallet `set-balance` torg check, 7a31297ec) passed (5 of 5 with the logins). They need `--env-var subRevampOtherTorgUserId=<user in another
    torg>` and `subRevampSameTorgUserId=<user with a wallet in the test torg>`, and money in the torg admin's wallet.
  - 350-368 (waive refused when short and rolled back, waive with createDue=false, plan change preview / stale 409 / change, allocated payment reversed so the
    due reopens, static-token cancel) passed on the second run (22 of 22 requests with the logins, 17 of 17 tests). They need
    `--env-var subRevampZeusTargetPlan=<a plan on a different cycle than the torg's current one>` and a billing that is unpaid with an empty wallet and advance.
    A stale expectedNetPayable gives a 409 with a message only; `data` is null (no preview body on `/plan-change`).
    A torg's second billing can be made without the scheduler with `POST /api/subscriptions/billings/start?torgId=` (it worked on an ACTIVE subscription).
  - Flags off: every flagged route refuses with body statusCode 403 and a message ending "is not enabled" / "are not enabled". The real HTTP status
    is 200 for all of them.

  ## Needs

  - A real VAHN_ADMIN login (OTP `776677`). Pass the phone at run time: `--env-var subRevampAdminPhone=<phone>`.
    Never commit it. Also pass `--env-var subRevampStaticToken=<VAHN_ADMIN static token>` (not stored anywhere) for
    steps 41, 51, 52, 56, 162, 233 and 237. The static token (zeus) is allowed on record/reverse external payment,
    move-to-wallet and partial charge (`requireRealUser` is gone); such actions are stored with null user ids and
    username `admin`. The real-login steps (43, 61, 72, 150, 163, 240 ...) store the signed-in admin's id and name.
  - A test torg. `subRevampTorgId`, `subRevampWalletId` (the torg admin's wallet), `subRevampPanId`, and
    `subRevampTorgAdminPhone` (a made-up number with no email, so no real person is contacted).
    Create it with admin calls (no DB access needed):
    1. `verify-otp` for a fresh phone, `POST /api/torgs` (name, torgAdminId = any user id), then
       `POST /api/users/torg/{torgId}` (role TORG_ADMIN, fresh phone: creates the admin AND its wallet) and
       `PUT /api/torgs/{torgId}` with `torgAdminId` = that new user.
    2. `POST /api/pan/without-verification` with `torgId` (PAN row; trucks need it to be verified manually).
    3. `POST /api/subscriptions/start?torgId=&planId=7&trialDays=0`, then `POST /api/subscriptions/trial?torgId=`
       and `POST /api/subscriptions/{torgId}/trial/extend?trialEndDate=<today>`. Plan 7 is monthly 99 + GST.
    4. `POST /api/trucks` x2 (`{registrationNumber, torgId}`, plates like MH69AB6901) and
       `PUT /api/trucks/mark-as-verified?panCardId=` for them: 2 verified trucks.
    5. `PUT /api/wallets/{walletId}/balance?amount=3000` (admin adjustment; there is no gateway-free deposit).
  - The hourly billing scheduler must create the first billing (nothing else creates it: `POST /billings/start`
    is broken for this, it reads `currentBillingDate`). Run 25-26 once it has.
  - Step 154 ends the trial again and the scheduler must bill the torg a second time (up to an hour). **Keep the flags OFF for that tick**:
    steps 157-173 expect the legacy-maths billing it makes then (wallet only, 1000 paid, advance untouched). With the flags on, the tick pays
    the whole billing from advance and 160-173 fail with 400. So close the window (step 300) after 153, run 154, wait, then run 30 and 155 onward.
  - Steps 10, 11 and 18 build URLs from the billing id: run 07 first.

  ## Order and state

  The flow is stateful and single-use per torg: B1 (plan 7, monthly) takes the external payments, a truck add-on,
  an upgrade and the first cancel. Steps 120-124 select a plan while no billing exists (TRIAL). B2 (half-yearly) is
  created by the scheduler and paid from advance only. A cycle change turns it into B3 (monthly) and back into
  advance, then B4 (half-yearly) is left short on purpose for the partial-charge cases and the PRO_RATA cancel.
  Plans on staging: 5 monthly 299 OPEN, 7 monthly 99 OFFERED, 8 annual 2028 OPEN, 11 half-yearly 1374 OPEN,
  9 annual 4800 OFFERED, 10 monthly 500 OFFERED and inactive. All prices exclude 18% GST.

  Variables are prefixed `subRevamp` because every plutus-api flow shares one environment file.
}
